## Done when

- [ ] Specs 47 (29 tests) and 46 (54) are green in Chrome against a fresh `build:e2e`.
- [ ] Before the CSS, 47 fails. Check this with `git stash push -m 2122-check -- apps/web/src`, rebuild, run, then `git stash apply` that entry and drop it.
- [ ] `pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck`, `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, `pnpm --dir e2e typecheck` and `pnpm exec eslint apps/web e2e` pass.
- [ ] `cargo jackioh spec index` has been run, and `cargo jackioh spec check` passes.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass.
- [ ] No `46` diff, no `.only` or `.skip`, and no `44px` added anywhere (use `var(--hit-min)`).
- [ ] The notes for the PR say `Closes #2122`, `Part of #2036` and carry one player note: `## Player note` / "On a phone, small buttons, links and fields take a tap across a whole fingertip."

## Risks

- **`position: relative` on every small control.** It could re-anchor an absolute descendant, or a static control's band could hang off an ancestor. The planner compared every element's box with the rule injected and without it on all 29 screens. Only three things moved: the pile icon, the "Reward" pill and the rarity dot (steps 2–4), and the stats table, which a `tr::before` re-laid out (hence `tr` is excluded). The audio toggle's `static` was the only explicit one (step 6). A control styled `position: static` later will get no band; spec 47 flags it only if it is on a measured screen.
- **Screens spec 47 does not see.** A dense list of short buttons may have bands that cover a neighbour by a few px. The creator's card list (4 px gap, about 30 px items) is one. Fix it the same way if it comes up; do not loosen the spec.
- **Daily suites.** With the CSS injected, the planner ran every component spec and e2e 03, 12, 23, 25, 27, 28 and 38 at phone size.
  - All passed except card-faces B15 (4 tests) and 38's `/practice (phone)` `target-size`.
  - Both failed the same way locally without the change.
  - Do not call either pre-existing on CI without a link (rule 12).
- **Smoke budget.** 47 adds about 35 s, spread over the two shards.
- **Rule 7.** The change is CSS and a spec only: nothing about game state.

## Open questions

None needs a person. These decisions were taken here and should be recorded in the PR:
- The rule applies under `(pointer: coarse), (max-width: 600px)`, index.css's existing finger query. Desktop is untouched.
- A small input or select takes `min-height` on the measured screens only, because they draw no `::before`.
- A checkbox or radio counts its labels.
- "Inline links" means `:is(p, label) a`, which includes the consent sentence.
- The spec also counts `::after`, which is the pile's existing band.
- The switch and the Activate badge stay narrower than 44 px on a phone tile: their split with the card's middle (B29) wins.
- Spec 47 joins `SMOKE`, so it runs before the PR merges itself.
- Other `44px` literals across the CSS stay as they are; only index.css's own rule moves to `--hit-min`.

